1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[roaring]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called…

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
I... give up!

14
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
-What?
-What?

15
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,000
[Leorio] Bastard!

16
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
I knew we shouldn’t have trusted you!

17
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
All you’re good for
is sabotaging the other applicants.

18
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
You’re just a worthless piece of garbage!

19
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
It took you long enough.

20
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
That’s what I do every year.

21
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
And I’ll keep on doin’ it
for as long as I can.

22
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
I don’t care
about passing the Hunter Exam;

23
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
I’m in it for the thrills.

24
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
BEWARE x OF x PRISONERS

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[narrator] The Third Phase of the Exam
is underway at Trick Tower,

26
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
where long-term prisoners are held.

27
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Gon and friends have chosen to partake
in a five-on-five battle

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
with some of the inmates.

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Thanks to Tonpa,
they’ve already suffered their first loss.

30
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,000
The next round
will pit Gon against Sedokan.

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Who knows what the upcoming battle
will bring?

32
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Now, then.

33
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
SEDOKAN
149-YEAR SENTENCE, SERIAL BOMBINGS

34
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
As you’ve all probably noticed,
I’m not terribly strong.

35
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,000
I don’t enjoy fighting, or running,
jumping, anything physical, really.

36
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
[Gon] I like that stuff a lot more
than thinking.

37
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
I guess I’ve never really been
all that great at using my head.

38
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
[Sedokan] I thought so.

39
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
So, I came up with a game.

40
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
One I think we’ll both enjoy.

41
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
-A game?
-[Sedokan] Yes.

42
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Yes. A simple game that doesn’t rely
on mental or physical activity.

43
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
What is it?

44
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
[Sedokan chuckles]

45
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
We each light a candle at the same time

46
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
and whoever’s candle goes out first
is the loser.

47
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
All right?

48
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Yep. Makes sense to me.

49
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
I’m in; let’s do it!

50
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
[Sedokan] Okay. In that case…

51
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
So which candle do you want to use?

52
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
It’s your choice.

53
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Press ‘O’ for the long candle

54
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
or press ‘X’ if you would rather have
the short one.

55
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Choose by majority rule.

56
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
So, we have to choose one?

57
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
This is a damn trap!

58
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Normally, you’d want to go
for the long one.

59
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Which means that low-life
must’ve done something to sabotage it!

60
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
[Kurapika]
Yes. That would be the safe assumption.

61
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
However, it could be a trick

62
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
and he’s actually tampered
with the short one.

63
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Hey, you’re right.
So, when you put it that way…

64
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Correct. There is no end.

65
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Sounds like you’ve got yourselves
a real dilemma.

66
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
You keep your big mouth shut!

67
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Yeah, yeah.

68
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Something happens when you’re presented
with an obviously biased choice:

69
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
suspicion mounts and
the decision-making process seizes up.

70
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Yes. This truly is a dilemma.

71
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Moreover,

72
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
the psychological impact
of making the wrong choice

73
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:59,000
is much greater than if the option
was between two evenly matched options.

74
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
[grumbles]

75
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
[smug chuckle]

76
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
[Sedokan] All right, then…

77
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Please, take all the time you need.

78
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
It’s a majority decision

79
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
but feel free to talk about it first.

80
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
No rush. We have plenty of time,
believe me.

81
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Hey! What should I pick?

82
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Dammit.

83
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Good question.

84
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
[chuckles]

85
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Gon! The choice is up to you!

86
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Pick whichever candle you think is best
is the best option.

87
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
That’s how we’ll all vote.

88
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Are you sure about this?

89
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
It’s just that
he doesn’t think things through.

90
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Instead of fretting over the choice,

91
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
let’s just put our faith
in Gon’s instincts.

92
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Trust his instincts, huh?

93
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Oh, I get to choose?

94
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
In that case

95
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
I’ll go with the long candle, okay?

96
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[smirks]

97
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
You want the long one?
Are you sure about that?

98
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Of course! The longer the candle,
the longer it burns.

99
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
It’s kind of a no-brainer.

100
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Well, that’s one way to look at it.

101
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
I told you he wasn’t gonna
think it through.

102
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Well. That settles it.

103
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[beep]

104
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Yeah, it’s not like
we’d be able to figure out

105
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
which one’s the trap, anyway.

106
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,000
[beep]

107
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[beep]

108
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,000
-[smirks]
-[beep]

109
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,000
[Sedokan] Okay!

110
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Looks like you get the long candle

111
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,000
and I’ll take the short one.

112
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
[metal grinding]

113
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
All right. Let’s light ‘em together.

114
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
[chuckles]

115
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
[chuckling]

116
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
[Killua] So, uh...

117
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Normally how long
would it take that candle to burn?

118
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
I would estimate five to six hours.

119
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[strong wind blowing]

120
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Oh, wow.

121
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
That sure was a close one.

122
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
[wind blows]

123
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,000
[Leorio] There’s a pretty strong wind
coming up from below.

124
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
They’ll have to stay still

125
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
and keep an eye on those flames.

126
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
There’s no chance
to let their guards down.

127
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
If you don’t pay attention
your candle will blow out.

128
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,000
[Gon] Yeah, I know.

129
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
That’s because you’re planning
to do something bad.

130
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Aren’t you?

131
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Otherwise, your short candle
would go out first.

132
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,000
I won't do anything.

133
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
‘Cause, you see...

134
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
I came prepared.

135
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
[startled cry]

136
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
[smirks] There. See?

137
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Hey. Take a look at Gon’s candle.

138
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
The flame suddenly got a lot stronger!

139
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,000
I should’ve known.

140
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
He somehow laced Gon’s candle
with gunpowder or some other accelerant.

141
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
That’s why it’s burning so much faster!

142
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
[Gon] Ow! Hot!

143
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
-[Killua] At this rate...
-[Gon] Hot...

144
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
[Killua] ...he’s only got another
two or three minutes!

145
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,000
[Leorio] Damn!

146
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Hey! That was a dirty trick!

147
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
I knew it! You messed with the long one,
didn’t you?

148
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
[smirks] You’re wrong.

149
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,000
I had four candles prepped and ready.

150
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
The disparate choice I presented you with

151
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,000
was merely camouflage
for the actual trap!

152
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:16,000
You assumed that one of the two
would be a trick candle.

153
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
The choices were so uneven

154
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
you never stopped
to consider the possibility

155
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
that I’d rigged both of them.

156
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:29,000
In the end it didn’t really matter
which of the candles you picked.

157
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Long or short…

158
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
I’d have handed you
an oil-soaked candle either way.

159
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
I guess now that the flame is
burning so much stronger…

160
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
it’ll take a lot more
than a little breeze to put it out.

161
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Hm?

162
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
He's fast!

163
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
[chuckles]

164
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
I win!

165
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Yes!

166
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
[solemn grunt]

167
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
[Lippo] Ooh.

168
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
That one’s got a real spring
in his step, doesn’t he?

169
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
And he knows how to take advantage
of a bad situation.

170
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Impressive. Very impressive.

171
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
[Gon] All right! I won!

172
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,000
You sure as hell did!

173
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
That’s one win for us!

174
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Once Kurapika and I win, we can advance!

175
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Idiot. That’s what you get
for relying on cheap tricks.

176
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Damn.

177
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
[hooded prisoner] Proper deception
calls for a little sacrifice.

178
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Watch and learn.

179
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
[loud clatter]

180
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
All right.

181
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
I’ll take the next one.

182
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,000
[roaring]

183
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:48,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

184
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,000
LIPPO

185
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
[prisoner cackling]

186
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
The next contender’s gotta face me!

187
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
MAJITANI
108-YEAR SENTENCE

188
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
MULTIPLE CRIMES,
INCLUDING FRAUD AND BLACKMAIL

189
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Man, that is one freaky body.

190
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Yeah. And face.

191
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Do ya see this, kid?

192
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:14,000
I’ve killed nineteen people so far.

193
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
But it’s such an uneven number.

194
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
To tell the truth, it kinda bugs me.

195
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
[snickering]

196
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
I’ve been lookin’ forward
to meeting number twenty for a while.

197
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[evil laughter]

198
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Oh, great.
We’re dealing with a serial killer?

199
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:35,000
[Majitani] The only way I’ll do this is
if we put our lives on the line.

200
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,000
It’s all or nothin’, do ya hear me, brat?

201
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Gimme blood!

202
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Spilling entrails!

203
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
And sweet agony!

204
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
[roaring in laughter]

205
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Oh yeah.

206
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
You must be terrified right now.

207
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,000
[Kurapika] Very well.

208
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
[Majitani] Huh?

209
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
You can decide how we settle this.

210
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,000
And I will accept it.

211
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,000
[Majitani chuckles]
You’ve got some balls, kid!

212
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,000
[scoffs]

213
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
But I know you’re quaking in your boots.

214
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
How long can you keep up
the tough guy act?

215
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Then you’re accepting a death match.

216
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,000
We go until one of us
either dies or admits defeat,

217
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
and not a second earlier, understand?

218
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,000
However…

219
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Don’t think admitting defeat or surrender
will stop me.

220
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Never has and, in fact, it never will,

221
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
so get it out of your head right now.

222
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:32,000
[maniacal laughter]

223
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Well?

224
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Scared stiff now, aren’t ya?

225
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
[Kurapika] Fine. I accept.

226
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Huh?

227
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Shall we begin?

228
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
[Majitani] What is he, an idiot?

229
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Didn’t he hear what I just said?

230
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
This is the real deal.
We’re fighting to the death!

231
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Wait, he should be trembling
just at the sight of me!

232
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Hold on! There’s something
I forgot to mention.

233
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Absolutely no weapons are allowed.

234
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
So, this has to be a simple fistfight.

235
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Even though I’ve been hired
as an Examiner,

236
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
I am still a prisoner.

237
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:16,000
And that means
that I’m not allowed to carry weapons.

238
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,000
That makes sense.

239
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,000
I understand.

240
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
It there anything else you forgot?

241
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
If not, I’d like to get started.

242
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
[Majitani grunts]

243
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
That little bastard!

244
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
He had a concealed weapon.

245
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
I’m glad I said something
before it was too late.

246
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,000
But from the look of it,
he doesn’t rely on it much.

247
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Is he really that confident
in his combat skills?

248
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
No. I don’t think its that’s it, either.

249
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:50,000
[derisive snort]
I bet he’s dying to run away

250
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:54,000
but he doesn’t want to look like a coward
in front of his friends.

251
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Or maybe he’s just so stupid

252
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
that he doesn’t comprehend how scary I am!

253
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
He can’t even wrap his head around it!

254
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:04,000
Yeah! Yeah, yeah, that’s gotta be it!

255
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[sinister grin]

256
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Well, in that case,

257
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:12,000
I’ve got a few cards up my sleeve
for dealing with fools like him.

258
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
[inhales deeply, grunts]

259
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
[flexing and grunting]

260
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
Hey, guys. Is Kurapika gonna be okay?

261
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,000
‘Cause if you ask me,
this guy looks pretty dangerous.

262
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
[Killua]
What looks so dangerous about him?

263
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
It’s obvious, well, to me, anyway,

264
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,000
that this guy’s a big talker.

265
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
He doesn’t have the guts to hit anybody,
let alone kill them.

266
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
-[Gon] I wouldn’t worry about it much.
-Huh?

267
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Why not?

268
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Because when I’m looking at him,
I don’t get chills or anything.

269
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
What does that mean?

270
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:02,000
I think it’s time
to show you my secret weapon!

271
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[roars]

272
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
The first of many!

273
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Here he comes!

274
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
[roaring]

275
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,000
[Kurapika grunts]

276
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Oh, my God.

277
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
He just punched a hole in the damn floor!

278
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
[Majitani] That was perfect.

279
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
And that’s not the only trick
up my sleeve.

280
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,000
[smirks]

281
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
[gasps]

282
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Look at his tattoo;
it’s a spider with twelve legs!

283
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,000
And that means...

284
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Yeah. I recognize it.

285
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Anybody who wants to be a Hunter

286
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
has heard all about tattoos like that one.

287
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:03,000
It’s the symbol worn by members
of that nefarious band of vicious thieves,

288
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
the Phantom Troupe!

289
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Really?

290
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Yeah. No doubt about it.

291
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Its meaning is widely known.

292
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
In fact, I-- I heard about them
straight from Kurapika.

293
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,000
[Majitani] Between the steel implants

294
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
that gives me the strength
to shatter rock with my bare hands

295
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
and the symbol of the Phantom Troupe...

296
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,000
they make one hell of a combo.

297
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Nobody would want to fight me
after getting a peek at those!

298
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
[Majitani laughing]

299
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,000
[Majitani] Aw, what’s wrong?

300
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Cat got your tongue?

301
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Name’s Majitani!

302
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
I’m one of the Phantom Troupe’s
four devas!

303
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
That first strike
was just an introduction.

304
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
This is your last chance to give up.

305
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
If you do, I’m still willing to...

306
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Huh?

307
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
[seething breathing]

308
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Hey... What’s wrong with you?

309
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
What are you...

310
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Huh?

311
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:27,000
[grunts]

312
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
[Majitani groaning]

313
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[strangled cries]

314
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[Majitani] Wait! Wait, I get it!

315
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Hold on, wait! Please don’t!

316
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
You win, okay?

317
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
[whistles]

318
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
[Kurapika] Take this to heart.

319
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,000
First,

320
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:11,000
a genuine Phantom Troupe tattoo
has the member’s number

321
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
inscribed on the spider’s back.

322
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Second,

323
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,000
they don’t bother tallying the people
they’ve killed

324
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,000
because it’s irrelevant to them.

325
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
And third,

326
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
don’t ever mention the Phantom Troupe
to me again.

327
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,000
If you do...

328
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,000
I will kill you with my bare hands.

329
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Oh, wow…

330
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Kurapika...

331
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Yeah. I saw that one
coming from a mile away.

332
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
[Leorio] Hey, are you okay?

333
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
[Kurapika] Yes. I’m not injured.

334
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
[Leorio] No, I mean,

335
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,000
is it safe for us
to be around you right now?

336
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
[Kurapika]
From the first moment I saw him,

337
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:24,000
I knew he wasn’t nearly
as powerful as he looked.

338
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
And in my mind,

339
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
I knew right from the start
that the tattoo was a fake.

340
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
But as soon as I saw that spider,

341
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,000
my vision went almost completely red.

342
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Well, nobody’s gonna blame you for that.

343
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
[Kurapika] To be perfectly honest…

344
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
-Huh?
-Huh?

345
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Whenever I see a spider, any spider,

346
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
all my rationale collapses
and I turn primal.

347
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:52,000
You should've told us.
Like, a long time ago.

348
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[Kurapika] That can only mean one thing.

349
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
The rage inside me
remains as strong as ever.

350
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,000
I suppose...

351
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
I should be happy.

352
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,000
I think we ought to keep Kurapika
away from any spiders, from now on.

353
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Oh yeah.

354
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
[Bendot] Damn you, Majitani.

355
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,000
You were completely worthless out there.

356
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Those facial scars on him
are from a botched plastic surgery.

357
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:20,000
That’s one hell of a fraud he pulled off.

358
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Okay. You know what’s happening, right?

359
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
After two losses, it’s do or die.

360
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,000
[hooded woman] I’ll handle it.

361
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:29,000
In fact, I know just the thing.

362
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,000
All right!

363
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Time for me to secure our victory!

364
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,000
[narrator]
With Kurapika’s triumph over Majitani,

365
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,000
they only need one more win

366
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
to clear the trial
and reach the next Phase.

367
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:53,000
But the question on all of their minds

368
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:56,000
is how will Leorio
handle the next challenge?

369
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
[theme song playing]

370
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Gon] Next time:
Trick To The Trick!

371
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,000
The trick to the trick is to trick...
I can't say it.

372
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[Killua] Say it properly!
